 18:"About 1% of the air. Used to fill light bulbs because it does not react.",
 19:"Your nerves and muscles need it. Bananas are a good source.",
 20:"Makes up your bones and teeth. Found in chalk, limestone and seashells.",
 22:"Strong and light. Used in airplanes, bike frames and medical implants.",
 24:"Gives stainless steel its shine and keeps it from rusting.",
 26:"The main element in steel. Iron rusts when it reacts with oxygen and water.",
 27:"Used to make strong magnets and blue glass.",
 28:"Used in coins, stainless steel and rechargeable batteries.",
 29:"Conducts electricity very well, so it is used in electrical wires.",
 30:"Coated on steel to keep it from rusting (galvanizing).",
 31:"A metal that melts at about 30 °C, so it can melt in your hand.",
 33:"Poisonous. Small amounts are used in electronics.",
 35:"One of only two elements that are liquid at room temperature. It is reddish-brown.",
 36:"A noble gas used in some flash lamps.",
 47:"Conducts electricity better than any other metal. Used in jewelry and electronics.",
